{
  "requirement": "The `habeas-requirements` skill MUST direct agents not to commit requirements or write implementation or test code until the user has agreed to, rejected, or deferred every group.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The requirement has one obligation. The `habeas-requirements` skill MUST direct agents not to commit requirements, and not to write implementation or test code, until the user has agreed to, rejected, or deferred every group.\n\n`tests/authoring_cli.rs#fn[the_requirements_skill_gates_commit_and_code_on_every_group_being_decided]` carries the `{test}` reference. It calls `assert_phrases(\"habeas-requirements\", ...)`. That calls `assert_text` on `bundled_skill(\"habeas-requirements\")`, which is `SKILL.md` plus its reference files with whitespace collapsed. `assert_text` asserts `text.contains(phrase)` and panics if the phrase is missing.\n\nThe asserted phrase is \"**Gate:** no implementation or test code, and no commit, until the user has agreed to, rejected, or deferred every group\". It covers each clause of the requirement:\n- no commit;\n- no implementation or test code;\n- the condition of agreed, rejected, or deferred;\n- the scope of every group.\n\nI read the skill's Workflow step in `assets/skills/habeas-requirements/SKILL.md`, which contains this Gate sentence. It matches the phrase, so the test would pass on the current text. If the gate were dropped, or weakened to leave out commit, code, or the rejected/deferred alternatives, the assertion would fail.\n\nThe requirement is about the text of the skill and does not name modes, boundaries, or failure cases. The step-ordering and commit-timing obligations belong to other requirements, such as `requirements.cli.requirements_review_skill.commit`, and are tested there. No gap found.",
